 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532562,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You want to install sod on one-half of your parallelogram-shaped backyard as shown. The patio covers the other half. Sod costs $50 a bag and covers <span data-math=\"25\\,{\\text{f}}{{\\text{t}}^2}.\">25\\,{\\text{f}}{{\\text{t}}^2}.</span> How much will it cost to buy the sod?\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/5e095ac6831a9a78.png\" alt=\"A parallelogram with a diagonal running from the top-left vertex to the bottom-right vertex. The region above the diagonal is shaded. The length and height of the parallelogram measure 25 feet and h equals 12 feet.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The area of a parallelogram with base <i>b</i> and height <i>h</i> is <span data-math=\"A = bh\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = bh = \\left( {{\\text{25 feet}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{12 feet}}} \\right) = 300{\\text{ f}}{{\\text{t}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>You are only covering half of the parallelogram, so you only need 150 square foot of sod.</p>\n<p>Make a conversion factor that uses the fact that sod costs $50 a bag and one bag covers 25 square feet.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"150\\cancel{{{\\text{f}}{{\\text{t}}^2}}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\$ 50}}{{{\\text{25 }}\\cancel{{{\\text{f}}{{\\text{t}}^2}}}}}} \\right) = \\$300\"></span></p>\n<p>The sod will cost $300.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$300"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
